# Later rules win, so the general case comes first and the exception after it.

# Source is normalised to LF in the repository and checked out however the
# platform prefers.
* text=auto

# The synthetic test corpus is DATA, not source code.
#
# Git must never translate line endings inside it. The corpus is byte-
# reproducible — `scripts/make_fixtures.py --check` compares SHA-256 digests,
# and `tests/fixtures/sample_repo/` has a pinned commit hash that only comes out
# the same if the files it commits are byte-identical. On Windows, git's default
# `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which changes both. That
# is what made every Windows test job fail on the first run CI ever performed.
tests/fixtures/** -text
